column1:
{"narrative": "Several months ago I opened a checking account with Citizens Bank based on a promotion in which I was to have direct deposits of a certain amount and would receive a cash bonus. I did receive the bonus. More recently I received an unsolicited email from Citizens Bank encouraging me to open a savings account. The headline and illustration showed three monthly deposits of at least {$25.00} would give me a bonus of {$25.00}. I received the promotional email on or about XX/XX/2022 and immediately opened the account and had a direct deposit of {$25.00} and set up a program wherein two additional deposits would be sent on the same day of the month to fulfill the requirement. Indeed I made three ( 3 ) monthly deposits of {$25.00} each for a total of {$75.00}. Citizens refused to grant me the {$25.00} bonus because I was apparently supposed to wait until XX/XX/2022 to make the deposits. 

Offer states it begins on XX/XX/2022. I did as requested and deserve the {$25.00}. 

Citizens personnel cut me off when I called, argued with me after I called back and gave me no relief."}

{"narrative": "I am writing to formally dispute the accuracy of a Discover Card account that appears on my credit file. This account does not belong to me. I have never applied for, opened, or authorized this account in any way. 



Under 15 U.S.C. 1681b, a consumer reporting agency may only furnish my credit report for specific, permissible purposes. Reporting an account that does not belong to me constitutes a violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act, as it does not meet the standard of accuracy and permissible use. 



I demand that this Discover CARD account be investigated and permanently removed from my credit file. Please provide written confirmation of your findings and the results of your investigation."}

{"narrative": "Chase Travel refuses to offer a difference in a price of a flight that was booked 4 days ago. 

All airlines will credit back vouchers for the difference and they state they can not. Even other travel agencies give refunds if prices drop. They stated to do a voucher I would then have XXXX $ taken from voucher when used. 

Flight is through XXXX  who said they would credit the money but couldn't since being through chase travel difference is XXXX $ in ticket price ( original fair purchased for XXXX $ new price XXXX $ ) ticket purchased on XX/XX/XXXX called for change on XX/XX/XXXX XXXX XXXX"}

{"narrative": "Once again filing a consumer finance dispute because I have run out of options here. XXXX will not give my money back and as of today, XX/XX/XXXX, they have stopped providing services to their user 's who prepaid A YEAR IN ADVANCE. I have filed this with XXXX as well. 

On XX/XX/XXXX- I sent XXXX an email asking for cancellation of my service. I wanted to see Wreck It Ralph and tried to, but the service would not issue me a ticket. Furthermore, I just checked my XXXX   account ( I can for some reason log-in online ) and I requested the cancellation before my " attempt '' is logged on the XX/XX/XXXX. I never saw Wreck it Ralph on the XX/XX/XXXX. I tried to see it on the XX/XX/XXXX,  but it obviously did not work out as you can see by the provided request for cancellation email. 

Then we go through the same things as noted before, XXXX never responds, XXXX never reinstates my account after multiple requests. I paid {$110.00} to watch 3 movies a month. I have been able to watch two movies : Spiderman on XX/XX/XXXX and Wreck it Ralph on XX/XX/XXXX. On top of everything else, XXXX charged me fees on top of the {$110.00} I paid to see these movies. I have already joined the lawsuit for this portion. I requested my cancellation well before seeing being able to see any movie. The only correspondence I have EVER received from XXXX was to let me know that this is my banks responsbility and they are deactivating my account. All documents with dates are attached. I have 7 months of service left. I have been unable to use this garbage service and {$110.00} is not some small amount of money. I work hard and this is totally unfair. They scammed thousands of users. Please Citi help me out! I use credit cards for the protection, so why is Citi not protecting me? Thank you!"}

{"narrative": "I am the author of this complaint. 

15 US Code 1681e states that every consumer reporting agency shall maintain reasonable procedures designed to avoid violations of section 1681c of this title and to limit the furnishing of consumer reports to the purposes listed under section 1681b of this title. I am not satisfied with my previous dispute because I have reason to believe that this company did not follow reasonable procedures when investigating the items that I disputed on my credit report, I believe that the company 's investigation was done by an automated eOscar system which is why the investigation yielded inaccurate and false information 15 US Code 1681i ( Section 5 paragraph A ) states that Treatment of inaccurate or unverifiable information ( A ) In general If, after any reinvestigation under paragraph ( XXXX ) of any information disputed by a consumer, an item of the information is found to be inaccurate or incomplete or can not be verified, the consumer reporting agency shall ( i ) PROMPTLY DELETE that item of information from the file of the consumer, or modify that item of information, as appropriate, based on the results of the reinvestigation ; and ( ii ) promptly notify the furnisher of that information that the information has been modified or deleted from the file of the consumer. From my understanding this company could be held liable for willful noncompliance under 15 US Code 1681n especially due to the statutory and actual damages i've suffered. 

The furnisher of the information is also liable under the FCRA under 15 USC 1681s-b ( 2 ) because they were notified of inaccurate and incomplete information on my report, and a proper reinvestigation was not done because the information is still inaccurate The fraudulent and incorrect accounts are listed below :"}

{"narrative": "I had a charge on my account that I did not recognize for services I had not receive. I disputed the charge with my credit card company ( Chase ) and they credited my account. The same merchant attempted to charge my card again twice separately after a six month and a one year hiatus. The last billing was in XX/XX/2019. 

I asked Chase to resolve this once and for all, and block this merchant as this is a repeated pattern. Chase analyzed past records, and agreed to block the merchant and stop all future billing and rebilling from this merchant. This assurance ( of account being credited and final resolution of the dispute along with blocking of the merchant for all future transactions on my account ) was first provided to me over the phone with Chase dispute resolutions representative, XXXX on XX/XX/2019 at XXXX. 

XXXX followed up with me with a letter stating the same ( attached ) where it clearly states, " We blocked this merchant from charging the account, you shouldn't see charges from this merchant on your account in the future. '' To my surprise, the same merchant charge was rebilled to my account in my XX/XX/XXXX statement. When I contacted Chase they were unwilling to resolve this. I shared the letter I received with XXXX and XXXX at Chase. XXXX said that the letter states that " you shouldn't see charges from this merchant '' does not mean " you will not see charges from this merchant. '' I asked XXXX if he is stating this on record and he said that the line is recorded and he stands by his statement that Chase 's prior commitment to block the merchant and that there will no charges is incorrect ( and therefore the charges remain )."}

{"narrative": "My name is XXXX XXXX - I live in XXXX, North Carolina. 

Someone has opened a credit card in my name with Citi CBNA - I have contacted the bank but they have not responded to me with via phone or online. I would like to find out how has used my social security to open this credit card.

I currently have a {$41.00} balance on this credit card and am not aware who used my social security to open this credit card."}

{"narrative": "On XX/XX/2020, I sent a letter regarding inaccurate and unknown information on my credit report. It has been over 60 days, and I have not received a response. I feel like Im being taken advantage of and being ignored for the dispute I requested. 

Section 611 ( a ), It is plainly stated : If the completeness or accuracy of any item of information contained in a consumers, or applicants, file at a consumer reporting agency ( such as XXXX  ) is disputed by the consumer. The consumer notifies the agency directly, or indirectly through a reseller, of such a dispute, the agency must, free of charge conduct a reasonable reinvestigation. This reinvestigation will determine whether the disputed information is inaccurate and record the status of the disputed information, or delete the item from the file. This must be done before the end of a 30-day period beginning on the date on which the agency receives the notice of the dispute from the consumer or reseller. 

It has been over 60 days. The inaccurate information/accounts should be deleted immediately, or I will file a litigation due to the stress it has cause me. My information was also impacted by the Equifax Data Breach and may have got into the hand of the wrong person."}

{"narrative": "Issue Type : Mortgage Loan Modification Deceptive or Unfair Terms Complaint Summary : I was offered a loan modification by Planet Home Lending on XX/XX/year>. The letter claims a 25 % principal reduction. However, the actual agreement includes : A balloon payment ( Partial Claim ) of {$160000.00} due at maturity A new loan balance of {$450000.00}, plus added legal and escrow charges A fixed 40-year term at 7.125 % interest, which is excessive This structure increases my total obligation to over {$620000.00}, which is more than my original loan amount of {$570000.00}. That is not a reduction its a repackaged increase with long-term financial risk. 

Additionally : No one contacted me to explain the terms I was given only two weeks to sign and return notarized documents No alternatives were offered I am now being told this is my only option, which feels coercive I am requesting : The balloon be eliminated The interest rate lowered The modification to reflect an actual principal reduction or affordable long-term solution This is not consistent with fair lending or loss mitigation standards. 



XXXX XXXX : Eliminate the balloon/partial claim Reduce the interest rate Provide a real principal reduction Extend the deadline to allow a proper review and negotiation"}

{"narrative": "Alliant Credit Union will not refund me GAP insurance refund when my car is paid off. 

XX/XX/XXXX : I purchased the vehicle and financed through the XXXX XXXX XXXX with GAP on the loan. Amount Financed : {$28000.00} XX/XX/XXXX : I refinanced the vehicle through Alliant Credit Union. The XXXX XXXX XXXX gave me the GAP refunds of unused premiums that I was entitled to receive, No problem. Amount Financed : {$27000.00} including the new GAP on Alliant Credit Union Auto Loan. 
XX/XX/XXXX : I refinanced the vehicle through XXXX XXXX XXXX but Alliant Credit Union refuses to give me pro-rated refund for the GAP. The payoff quote for {$25000.00} from Alliant Credit Union was not reduced by any refunds of unused premiums that I am entitled to receive. I called Alliant Credit Union multiple times to obtain the GAP pro-rated refund since I paid off my loan early/refinance but Alliant Credit Union still insists on stating that the GAP is non-refundable regardless of the fact that the loan is paid off early. Alliant Credit Union Loan Department doesn't reply to my emails."}

{"narrative": "I am writing to formally request a detailed description of the procedures your agency used to verify the accuracy and completeness of the information currently under dispute, as required by 15 U.S.C. 1681i ( a ) ( 7 ) Method of Verification.

Under this provision, I have the right to receive a complete explanation of the reinvestigation process, including the name, address, and, if reasonably available, the telephone number of any furnisher of information that was contacted regarding the disputed item.

Please ensure this information is provided within 15 days of receiving this request, in accordance with your obligations under federal law."}

{"narrative": "NationStar Mortgage is the only lender out of the XXXX other lenders that I have that give me issues. For about a year they kept calling me and harassing me about payments being late on the XXXX of each month, when in fact I had till the XXXX to make the payment. After a year of calling an yelling at them over the phone they stopped. Thank XXXX some law firm filed a class action against them which I was more than happy to sign up. 

2- They changed my bill to paperless. I have called multiple times about them changing it back to bill. 

3- My Adjustable rate expired and they never notified me that my payments had gone up. They assumed I would log in online and see it. I did not receive anything in mail 4- Every year, the harass me about my home insurance policy, they want to force their own policy on to me and they can not figure out my name after 7 years still."}

{"narrative": "Capital One received my paycheck on Wednesday night, as verified by my employer. 
Friday afternoon, and my account still is XXXX after CApital one removed any and all funds to cover a bill that was valid. My direct deposit is still not there. The amount of my paycheck should be {$3500.00}. 

I called my employer who verified the deposit had left their account. Capital one will no longer take my calls, nor provide any info as to how much longer my delay will be."}

{"narrative": "On XX/XX/2020, I made a purchase from " XXXX ''. The company 's website clearly indicated that the item would be shipped within 5 days. However, I reached out for a status update on XX/XX/XXXX, via email and XXXX ( per website contact method ) and by email again, on the XXXX, but never received a return response. 

Also, the product that I received, appeared to have been used. Upon arrival, all four corners of the box were mashed in and deeply scratched beyond the surface and deep scarring appeared along the edges of the box as well. There were multiple layers of packaging tape, that had turned yellow, which indicates age & that the box had possibly been re-sealed due to multiple returns. I understand that mild damage is to be expected during shipping but the type of damage described is indicative of extensive wear & tear, over a period of time, not from a one time transaction. The item that I purchased was for an inflatable life raft. So, for obvious reasons, I am not comfortable in accepting a second hand product in which safety checks have not been conducted, directly by the manufacturer, resulting in potentially fatal consequences for myself and my family. 

I tried twice, to resolve this issue with my credit card company by submitting complete and detailed documentation to support the dispute that I'd filed. The merchant responded to the dispute by forwarding a copy of the transaction and other random, meaningless pages that did not address the issues of my complaint. Afterwards, I received a letter from my credit card company stating that I did not furnish sufficient information to support my dispute, therefore, my case was being closed and I was advised to circle back to the merchant for further resolution."}

{"narrative": "We submitted a Qualified Written Request ( QWR ) and Debt Validation Letter ( DVL ) to Nationstar Mortgage LLC ( XXXX Mr. Cooper ) via certified mail on XX/XX/XXXX. These letters were received on XX/XX/XXXX. The QWR requested validation of debt, servicing history, investor information, and chain of title documentation. As of this filing, no proper response to the QWR has been provided. Instead, Nationstar filed foreclosure on XX/XX/XXXX ( XXXX XXXX, Florida, Case No. XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX ), during the open QWR window, in what appears to violate RESPAs dual tracking restrictions ( 12 CFR 1024.41 ( g ) ). 

In XXXX, we also submitted a negotiable instrument for $ XXXX than the loan balanceto resolve the account. Nationstar retained this instrument but did not acknowledge or apply it. Additionally, public records show the mortgage assignment was recorded more than three years after the loan originated, breaking the chain of title. The note bears a pay to the order of [ redacted ] without recourse endorsement, suggesting it was transferred without proper disclosure. Multiple investor payoffs appear in the servicer 's payment history, indicating the loan may have been settled or sold without our knowledge. Despite this, Nationstar continues to demand payment and proceed with foreclosure. 

We request a full investigation into these practices, which appear deceptive, noncompliant, and potentially unlawfulespecially considering this is a VA-backed loan."}

{"narrative": "I have spoken to 4 different individuals in their Credit Card fraud team and was told that the phone call was being recorded.

I was denied access to speak to a manager.

I was also told by the last person that they can not provide the address whereby the calls can be subpoenaed because it was a security issue for them. Priceless. What is Chase ( JPM ) hiding?"}

{"narrative": "I have called the 3 credit reporting agencies multiple times, Experian, XXXX XXXX to please correct the personal information on my account. The have not corrected the inaccurate information they are reporting. 

I have called and spoken to several representatives and supervisor and they have not yet corrected my personal information. 

I called on XXXX, XXXX, XXXX, XXXX."}

{"narrative": "I am submitting this complaint under FCRA 605B ( 15 U.S.C. 1681c-2 ) because my personal information was compromised in the XXXX  data breach. As a result, fraudulent accounts and hard inquiries are now appearing on my credit report.

These include, but are not limited to : Personal credit card ( s ) auto loan ( s ) Personal loan account ( s ) One or more collection accounts and multiple hard inquiries I did not authorize I did not open or authorize any of these accounts or inquiries. I have attached my FTC Identity Theft Report as proof.

I am requesting that all fraudulent accounts, collections, and inquiries related to the XXXX  data breach be permanently removed from my credit file within 4 business days in accordance with FCRA 605B"}

{"narrative": "I have a credit card with Cominity BankXXXXXXXX XXXX # XXXX. The first time I used the card I made a purchase on XX/XX/XXXX for {$77.00}. When I tried to make a payment on or about XX/XX/XXXX, the website would not let me set up an online account. When I tried to make a phone payment, the calls kept on getting dropped/disconnected. On or about XX/XX/XXXX, I received a call from Comenity and I made the payment in full with the agent. I asked about the late fee and was told that they could see I had attempted to login and they would remove the late charge. Next statement I was charged a late fee of {$30.00}. In XXXX, I tried to call them but the only options they gave me on the phone was to make an automated payment. Now, with another late fee the balance was {$63.00}. Same thing for XXXX, XXXX and XXXX, with late fees of {$40.00}, {$44.00} and {$45.00}. 

On XX/XX/XXXX, I sent a letter to Cominity telling them of my difficulty trying to connect with an agent and asking for all these charges to be removed, as they had originally agreed. On XX/XX/XXXX, I received another statement with another {$46.00} added on to the balance, bringing the balance up to {$230.00}. 

I was finally able to reach a customer service agent on XX/XX/XXXX, after three disconnections/dropped calls in the process. They refused to remove the original {$30.00} fee that they had agreed to back in XXXX and would not remove any of the other late fees. They told me that if I didn't pay the full balance now an additional {$50.00} late fee would be assessed next week. I spoke with a supervisor, who offered that if I paid {$150.00}, they would remove the rest and close the account. I paid them {$150.00} to avoid further gouging."}

{"narrative": "After months of looking on the AES Success website for a mechanism to pay down the principle on my student loan, I finally chatted a customer service representative to ask. 

The individual informed me that I had to ASK for that feature to be turned on, otherwise, my overpayments would always go toward my next payment amount and the company could continue charging interest on the overall principle. 

If not illegal, this practice is immoral! AES Success should be ashamed of themselves and they should be forced to give clients an option with each payment as other lenders do!"}

{"narrative": "Last week I applied for a used car loan at my financial institution, USAA. I asked for a loan up to {$15000.00} but also told the loan processer at USAA that I hoped I would need a loan for less than $ 15K after we finished negotiations on the car. I was quoted a rate of 2.75 % for this loan. 
After concluding negotiations with the owner of the vehicle for the sale at {$13000.00}, I gave the owner my personal check for {$1000.00}, so the remainder needed for a loan was {$12000.00}. I called USAA to execute the loan, but was told that for any amount less than $ 15K, the interest rate would be higher than 2.75 %. Because of the higher rate, I complained and spoke to several different people in USAA 's loan department, resulting in rates quoted from 4.75 % down to 3.2439 %. They still refused to give me the rate originally quoted of 2.75 %, even though I have a screen printed from their website showing the 2.75 % rate for my loan. They claimed that if I would take the $ 15K ( or higher amount ) loan, I could still get the 2.75 % rate, but for any lesser amount, the rate would be higher. This makes no sense at all, since their risk for a smaller loan amount is less than with the larger loan amount. 

This is nothing more than a classic " bait-and-switch '' tactic. If this was a disreputable loan shark, I might understand their tactic, but for USAA, I did n't expect such dishonorable and dishonest behavior. They should be prosecuted for their " bait-and-switch '' tactic to the fullest extent of the law."}

{"narrative": "They are saying I owe XXXX XXXX XXXX. I've never had an account with them. I've tried to get the original contact information but no one has it. They're gon na garnish my check. 

They want me to file fraud information but they wont give me any information on the original account. 

The company name is XXXX XXXX XXXX"}

{"narrative": "Wells Fargo closed XXXX of my XXXX plus accounts I have with them because they said i don't have a physical address with them ( which i did ). They then sent a check for {$8600.00} to my physical address! I don't get mail at my physical address. i have called them multiple times spending hours on the phone. I asked for a XXXX to call me, which they said they would have someone call me within XXXX hours, which of course i never got the call. It's been over a week since the promised of a phone call. 
I want my money back with 5 % interest for the time they have confiscated it. 

my filed complaint with them is XXXX"}

{"narrative": "On XX/XX/2022, my card was charged {$660.00} instead of {$65.00} when in XXXX. When I got back to America I disputed the charge on XX/XX/XXXX. They got back to me XX/XX/XXXX saying they were researching the dispute and on XX/XX/XXXX they confirmed the transaction was valid. I put in a dispute again the day after, and on XX/XX/XXXX they began researching again, and found the charges valid. On XX/XX/XXXX, I disputed again, told me they were researching XX/XX/XXXX, and confirmed they were valid XX/XX/XXXX. In XXXX I filed a dispute again, XXXX XXXX  XXXX they said they were researching, XX/XX/XXXX they said they believed my dispute, but too much time has passed so they couldnt give me my money back. 

The charge happened on XX/XX/2022 when I was in XXXX. I was at XXXX XXXX XXXX restaurant for lunch where my bill was XXXXXXXX EGP ( {$65.00} USD ). I handed the waiter my card and bill, he charged me XXXX EGP ( {$660.00} ). They then took my friends card and billed her the correct amount of {$65.00}. After many failed attempts with Chase Bank, I contacted the restaurant over XXXX XXXX in XXXX. They immediately replied and said they have the receipt right here, sent me the receipt, then sent me a bank statement. This bank statement was them transferring the XXXX EGP to a bank account under the name XXXX XXXX I am not him. 

I still have all the receipts and conversations with the restaurant if needed."}

{"narrative": "AWA is trying to collect on a debt, that was initially settled prior. In agreement with original company XXXX XXXX XXXX. This is a XXXX XXXX. In which, account was suppose to be an {$500.00} pay-off at the Primary account holders time of released ( 2018 ). 

It was agreed to pay two payments of {$250.00}, that was paid prior to collections. In addition, I was not suppose to be the co-signer of this bond. My bank information was only suppose to be used to pay this debt/bond in full at the time of service. Furthermore, this bond is on a case that was never committed or fault, or guilt. 

XXXX XXXX XXXX and AWA Collections. Refused to acknowledge such agreement. I feel my rights and personal information was used to furnish this debt/bail and that original company completely mishandled, mislead, and fraudulently obtained my information. If In fact, I legally owe this. I am requesting the right to properly dispute. As again, I was unaware of such matter."}

{"narrative": "XXXX XXXX XX/XX/2024 LVNV Funding LLC XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX, SC XXXX Re : XXXX Dear LVNV Funding LLC, I am responding to your communication about a debt youre trying to collect. You contacted me by Mail and identified the debt as {$720.00} Please send the following information : The name and address of the original creditor, the account number and the amount owed Verification that there is a valid basis for claiming I am required to pay the current amount owed Details about the age and amount of the debt including a copy of the last billing statement from the original creditor A detailed explanation of any interest added or payments made since the last billing statement and the legal authorization for this interest The date the original creditor claims this debt became delinquent Whether this debt is within the statute of limitations and how that was determined Please also forward details about your authority to collect this debt : Include whether you are licensed in my state, and if so, provide the date of the license, name on the license, license number, and the name, address and telephone number of the state agency issuing the license. If you are contacting me from outside my state, provide the licensing information from your state as well. 

Thank you for your cooperation. 

Sincerely, XXXX XXXX"}

{"narrative": "On XXXX XXXX, 2016, I sold a condo to folks who previously had rented the property from me ( XXXX XXXX and XXXX XXXX ). As part of the purchase contract, I paid the closing costs. As part of the final Settlement Statement, the mortgage loan officer and the closing agent stated by phone and email that if we did not purchase the " optional '' owner 's title insurance policy that the price of the lender 's title policy would increase proportionally. In effect, this practice forces the purchase of a product ( the owner 's title policy ) to the detriment of consumers. I am seeking a refund of this cost ( {$270.00} ) and for regulatory intervention by the CFPB to consider ending a practice that is unfair to consumers. 

The purchasers have given me authorization to file this complaint on their behalf. Thank you for your assistance! 

XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXXXXXX"}

{"narrative": "The Fair Credit

Reporting Act ( 15 U.S. Code 1681 ) says ( 1 ) The banking system is dependent upon fair and accurate credit reporting. Inaccurate credit reports directly impair the efficiency of the banking system, and unfair credit reporting methods undermine the public confidence which is essential to the continued functioning of the banking system. So whenever there is a violation under the FCRA, it impairs the efficiency of the banking system. This is a violation of my privacy with my consumer report, since I control what is listed and what is not. In the event that any accounts are reported without my written consent, that is considered identity theft. This is a violation of both 15 U.S. Code 1681b ( 2 ) and 15 U.S. Code 1681c-2. This leads way to civil liability against the credit reporting agency for negligent and willful noncompliance under 15 U.S. Code 1681n, which allows for {$XXXX} per violation, for account listed without my express
ed written consent."}

{"narrative": "This account by CARECREDIT was introduced by XXXX XXXX for 100 % finance for the multifocal lens implant so I could take the unnecessary surgery on XX/XX/. 
It resulted more problems on my left eye, instead of improving the vision as XXXX XXXX presented prior to the XXXX. I paid the XXXX installment and stopped further as I learned that the XXXX caused more damage than ever on my left eye. 

* Please refer to the details from the attached complaint made by me ( XXXX XXXX, patient )"}

{"narrative": "My name is XXXX XXXX DOB XX/XX/86. I have been impacted with COVID SINCE XXXX! I HAVE BEEN IN CONTAXT WITH XXXX  WHEN NOT on XXXX  as I could. I have been in most recent contact, XXXX, XXXX, XXXX and XXXX Each month aside from XXXX, I was told, my account was covered under the assistance program for COVID AND NO PAYMENT WAS DUE. I THEN GET A COLLECTION CALL IN XXXX STATING I OWE {$190.00}!!! They told me all this missed COVID PAYMENTS WERE NOW ALL DUE AT ONCE!!! I HAD NO NOTICE THIS WOULD BE THE CASE, NO WRITTEN AGREEMENT NOTHING!!! THIS IS UDAAP!!! HOW CAN A PERSON IMPACTED BY COVID PAY ALL THESE PAYMENTS AT ONCE!! WELL DUE TO MY CONCERNS WITH MY CREDIT SINCE MY HUSBAND JUST DIED FROM COVID AND SO DID MY DAUGHTER, I NEED MY CREDIT! SO I SOLD MY WEDDING BAND TO COVER BILLS! THIS BILL! I PAID {$200.00}!!! TWO DAYS LATER MY CREDIT SCORE DROPS 33 POINTS! WHY?! BECAUSE XXXX  REPORTED ME PAST DUE!! I CALLED IN AND THE THRIRD PARTY REP TOLD ME ITD BECAUSE I HAVE NOT MADE A PAYMENT SINCE XXXX. I TOLD HIM I WAS TOLD I DID NOT HAVE TO BECAUSE I WAS ON TEH COVID PLAN. HE SAID, WELL I SEE THEY WAIVED LATE FEES FOR THOSE MONTHS, BUT I STILL HAD TO MAKE PAYMENTS - XXXX  XXXX!!! TOTAL XXXX!! I WAS TOLD I DID NOT HAVE TO! 

THEY NEED TO BE INVESTIGATED FOR HOW THEIR TREATING COVID IMPACTED CUSTOMERS!! THEY TOLD ME I QUALIFIED FOR COVID ASSISTANCE, AND NO AYMENTS WERE DUE, THEN THEY DEMAND A {$190.00} PAYMENT WITH NO NOTICE AT ALL!!! THERE WAS NO AGREEMENT TO MAKE ME AWARE THAT COULD HAPPEN! 

I NOW HAVE TO CREMATE MY DAUGHTER WHO DIED FROM COVID BECAUSE THESE CARELESS XXXX  RUNIED MY CREDIT!!! I COULD NOT AFFORD NOR GET A LOAN TO GIVE HER A PROPER FUNRAL!! THEY NEED TO BE HELD ACCOUNTABLE FOR THIS!!!"}

{"narrative": "XX/XX/XXXX - received email notice from affirm about loan with XXXX XXXX. I called at XXXX on XX/XX/XXXX immediately after receiving the email and notified them they the loan was fraudulent. They assured me the loan would not be processed and my account would be locked. I called again at approx XXXX again to verify that my dispute went thru and my the fraudulent affirm card/loan was blocked. 

XX/XX/XXXX - received email at XXXXXXXX XXXX  that the fraudulent affirm card was available even though Affirm assured me on XX/XX/XXXX that the loan and card would not be processed and the originator XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX XXXX XXXX, UT XXXX would be notified of the fraud. 

They never notified the loan originator XXXX XXXX in XXXX XXXX XXXX Utah of the fraud. When finally speaking wuth an Affirm supervisor XXXX XXXX, he actively discouraged me from calling the originator and reporting the fraud on my own. I then asked Affirm to provide me with their FDIC number so i could file a complaint and they could not provid one, I asked for information so I could file a police report where the crime occurred and they could not provide that information. I asked for phone logs because loan approvals are verified using multifactor authentication and they would not provide that information. I asked for the email explaining the data breech that took place earlier this month XXXX, XXXX and affirm would not provide that. In my opinion, because XXXX is not an FDIC insured entity, Affirm acquires no risk with regards to these loans and therefore actively profits from the administrative policy and limiting information to their customers regarding fraudulent charges and loans approved in their names."}

{"narrative": "XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX ( XXXX XXXX XXXX ) to me XXXX closed my brokerage account years ago due to a small negative balance ( ~ {$21.00} ). Recently, XXXX support emailed me and confirmed in writing that the negative balance was forgiven, the restriction was removed, and I could reactivate my account through the app ( they instructed : Account Menu Settings Reactivate Account ). 

Quote from XXXX support ( attached screenshot ) : The deficit was forgiven and resolved I was able to remove the original restriction If youd like to reactivate your account, you can request to do so directly in your app. 



When I followed their instructions, the app displayed a conflicting message : This account is closed. Your XXXX account was permanently closed, and it cant be reopened. ( attached screenshot ). I have attempted to resolve this via in-app support, email, and phone for several weeks, but XXXX written XXXX and system behavior contradict XXXX another, and I remain blocked from reactivation. XXXX also attempted and failed to update my legal name while my account was restricted ( evidence of a system-level block ). I need resolution : I want my account reactivated as XXXX stated in writing. If they refuse, I request written confirmation that the account is permanently closed, the balance is {$0.00}, and that no credit reporting or collections will occur."}

{"narrative": "I am writing in regards to the closure of my checking and savings accounts due to alleged fraud on the associated checking account. To the best of my knowledge, no investigation has been conducted in this matter. 

Subsequent to my inquiry about the case, the funds within the checking account were mailed to me. However, I have not received any updates on the savings account despite receiving a mail stating a balance of {$500.00}. 

I have made multiple attempts to contact the bank for clarification on the matter but have not received a satisfactory response. I would greatly appreciate your prompt assistance in resolving this issue and retrieving the funds from my savings account"}

{"narrative": "Navy Federal was my main bank so I just thought that the extra fees that I got charged per purchase was just their policy but with my other bank accounts it didnt work that way. I actually got to a point where I was tired of all the fees I removed my direct deposit for a while.

As Im currently writing this, I had the funds in my account, but received a negative balance. 

In the XXXX of XXXX XXXX, I received and several charges for fees on returned payments and majority of the time, there were funds in the account but due to the delay in processing payments, it led to a clashing and the fees were costing me more returned fees. Its all so overwhelming."}

{"narrative": "I received a preapproval offer for a loan of {$10000.00} for 36 months at an interest rate of 18.99 %. I found this offer appealing as I needed extra cash to get through the holidays and planned to repay it after the new year. 

However, I was shocked to discover that the company funded me for only {$9000.00} instead of the promised {$10000.00}. Upon reviewing the loan paperwork, which I only received after the funds were deposited, I noticed a {$1000.00} loan origination fee that I never agreed to. This fee significantly alters the terms of the loan and increases my interest rate beyond the initially quoted 18.99 %. 

I also attempted to obtain a Truth in Lending statement but received a document that only contained my name and an IP address, without any legitimate signatures or terms. I never signed any documents agreeing to this loan or its terms, and I am concerned that this practice is illegal."}

{"narrative": "XXXX is the last complaint I filed with you regarding this company. Even after I filed this complaint they did not investigate or validate this debt. This debt is not mine and I have never seen the provider listed on the I voice. Sending me an invoice for a provider I've never seen does not make the debt mine. And thar very invoice shows a XXXX  balance yet it's being reported otherwise. 

The credit bureaus decided that by mid XXXX, medical debt less than {$500.00} will no longer appear on credit reports run by XXXX, XXXX or XXXX. Yet despite this debt not being mine, validated, not having written consent and being under {$500.00} in the year XXXX  this company is illegally reporting it. This is abusive. So SCA Collections is in violation of the FCRA and XXXX. 

If this fraudulent account is not removed, I will contact the Attorney General and also hold SCA Collections financially responsible for all charges I incur from higher interest rates due to the reporting of this fraudulent account and blatant refusal to remove it. This is defamation of character."}

{"narrative": "On XX/XX/2020, I paid off my Bank of America AAA credit card. I paid the balance off and in full. The balance was {$2900.00}. 

When I got my statement which was for the period XX/XX/XXXX - XX/XX/2020, it had an interest charge of {$30.00}. The date of the interest charge was XX/XX/2020. 

I talked to customer service but I still do not understand how if I pay the balance off in full, they can continue to charge me interest."}

{"narrative": "I have repeatedly contacted Discover. My card was stolen and they setup an XXXXXXXX XXXX account. Discover did refund historical charges but refuses to block new recurring charges. XXXX tells me they card is active and associated with an account and because Im not on the account they cant remove it. Neither party is willing to fix this. Basically every month Im going to have to contact discover to dispute a new XXXX recurring charge. Since its recurring, they say theres nothing they can do about it. 

I first contacted approx XX/XX/XXXX when I saw the charges. On XX/XX/XXXX was my most recent call. I told them explicitly if this is not resolved Ill contact CFPB. They reiterated they set up a block for new charges but arent able to block recurring charges. On XXXX XXXX charged me TWICE for XXXX for XXXX, and theres a XXXX statement credit on XXXX that I guess was automatically triggered. I cant get Discover or XXXX to stop fraudulent charges. 

I cant get them to stop. Please help me."}

{"narrative": "I noticed that my FHA mortgage account is being reported with a balance of {$510000.00} and showing multiple late payments, including 30-day, 60-day, and 90-day past due statuses. The account reflects several late payments and a past due amount, even though I disputed this information. 

Despite the dispute, the account continues to be reported as 90 days delinquent, and the dispute is not clearly reflected. The late payment history being reported does not seem accurate or consistent with my understanding of the account. 

I contacted the mortgage servicer and requested a review of this information, but the reporting has not been corrected. There are also inconsistencies in how the payment history and dates are shown, which adds to the confusion."}

{"narrative": "The XXXX account is a prepaid account, and I do not have any pending balance with them. I have no active debt or overdue amount related to XXXX. 

