{"narrative": "My husband and I spoke to multiple people on the phone from Navy Fed XX/XX/XXXX after being scammed and lost {$2500.00}. The last person we spoke to had told us a fraud claim was going to be made. They explained to us the process and told us that if the claim was approved, we would receive our money back from Navy Fed. If the claim was not approved, we could provide supporting documentation and have our claim investigated again. We later followed up and were told our claim was approved and we had to wait ten business days for our money to go back into our account. 

I had not seen any money returned to our account, so I called navy fed on XX/XX/XXXX. They told us that the claim was declined, and that whoever described the process to us before was misleading or untrue. When asked if we could contact the person that had told us this information, we were told that's not possible. I was then told that information like this can not be discussed over the phone and that I had to message in my account. That same day I messaged in my Navy Federal account the whole situation. They finally followed up with me XX/XX/XXXX. Simply put, they stated " we are unable to assist you ''. 

My husband and I never took actions such as contacting law enforcement or making a report because we were confident Navy Fed was going to help us through this. We are disappointed in the utmost."}

{"narrative": "I have been using the Discover It cashback card for over a year now. I and my friend got it almost at the same time. He recently told me that he received a retention offer from Discover : 3 % additional cashback on all purchases upto {$2500.00}. I asked him how he got it and he explained the process in detail. I called in Disccover customer service to check if I have similar offers but the representative said I dont have any offers on my card. I requested if there is lower valued offer available but she confirmed I have none. I told her that I have used the card responsibly in the past one year, I have used the card so much that I had maximised all the 5 % rotating cashback categories and aim to keep using the card. I have been a loyal member of the card by making no late or missed payments. My friend on the other hand uses the card less than what I do and has a lesser accumulated cashback than I do. The representative was apathetic and reluctant to listen and didnt give any offers to me. 

Not only this, my friend also got targeted offers from Discover during the first year .. a cashback offer on XXXX and another elevated cashback offer on restaurants. But I never receive such offers. 

The above incidents clearly represent motivated hate against me resulting in disproportionate discrimination."}
